Sent to Will Reid

The Science of Consciousness (TSC) is an interdisciplinary conference empha=
sizing rigorous approaches to the study of consciousness and its place in t=
he universe. Topical areas include neuroscience, philosophy, psychology, co=
gnitive science, biology, quantum physics and quantum brain biology, cosmol=
ogy, meditation, altered states, artificial intelligence/machine consciousn=
ess, the nature of reality, culture and experiential phenomenology.
TSC Conferences since 1994<https://consciousness.arizona.edu/science-consci=
ousness-conferences>
The Science of Consciousness - Past Conferences
The Science of Consciousness (TSC) conferences  are the pre-eminent world g=
atherings on all approaches to the profound and fundamental question of how=
 the brain produces conscious experience, a question which addresses who we=
 are, the nature of reality and our place in the universe.   TSC conference=
s<https://consciousness.arizona.edu/science-consciousness-conferences> have=
 been held in Tucson since 1994, (every 2 years) and are recognized around =
the world. TSC International held its first conference in 1995 and continue=
s in alternate years.
