Stuart Hameroff=92s research pursued microtubule information processing and=
 anesthetic action. In the mid-1990s he teamed with eminent British physici=
st and Nobel Laureate Sir Roger Penrose to develop a controversial quantum =
theory of consciousness (=91orchestrated objective reduction=92, =91Orch OR=
=92) based on microtubule quantum computing. Harshly criticized initially, =
Orch OR is now supported by experimental results including anesthetic actio=
n. In 2017, with Sir Roger Penrose, James Tagg, Ivette Fuentes and Erik Vii=
erre, Hameroff co-founded the Penrose Institute, intended to support resear=
ch based on the various works of Sir Roger (cosmology, quantum mechanics, g=
eneral relativity, black holes, geometry and consciousness).
